{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8226862",
      "title": "Preparing Another Problem That Can Be Fixed with useEffect",
      "sourceHash": "f6ed19cab03f5b86f1c925e9665141ffe6ced5c408cf464b8e73e04392493903",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.25,
          "end": 3.657,
          "en": "Now besides this dependencies array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.657,
          "end": 8.657,
          "en": "useEffect also has one other feature you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "And for this feature, let's go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 14.403,
          "en": "to this delete confirmation component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 18.956,
          "en": "This component is responsible for rendering the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.956,
          "end": 21.583,
          "en": "of this modal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.583,
          "end": 25.333,
          "en": "And I now want to add a feature to this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.333,
          "end": 30.333,
          "en": "where this modal closes automatically after three seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.958,
          "end": 33.72,
          "en": "and we automatically delete the place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "so we automatically confirm this modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 38.673,
          "en": "after those three seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.77,
          "end": 44.623,
          "en": "And to implement this feature, we need to set a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.623,
          "end": 49.14,
          "en": "which we can do with help of another browser feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.14,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "the set timeout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 55.053,
          "en": "which is a function built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 59.25,
          "en": "Set timeout takes two arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.25,
          "end": 62.49,
          "en": "and the first argument is a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.49,
          "end": 66.75,
          "en": "The second argument is a duration in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.75,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "For example, 3000 milliseconds would be three seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "And this function, which you pass as a first argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 79.53999999999999,
          "en": "will be executed once this duration expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.53999999999999,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "So if we want to close this modal after three seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 89.53999999999999,
          "en": "we should call onConfirm inside of this callback function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 92.834,
          "en": "that executes after three seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 92.834,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "so that when this component is rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 99.33,
          "en": "this timer here is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 99.33,
          "end": 104.33,
          "en": "and we then execute onConfirm after three seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now with this code, we'll face a couple of problems though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 113.96000000000001,
          "en": "One problem is that this delete confirmation component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 114.09,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "is always rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "It is rendered here by the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "and it's wrapped by the modal component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "which is also always rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 128.3,
          "en": "it's just not always visible in the DOM because internally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 128.34,
          "end": 132.66,
          "en": "the modal component controls the dialogue's visibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 132.66,
          "end": 137.66,
          "en": "through this open prop by showing or hiding this dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 141.39,
          "en": "But technically this delete confirmation component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 143.43,
          "en": "is always part of the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 147.74099999999999,
          "en": "and therefore this timer will actually be set and started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 147.74099999999999,
          "end": 151.11,
          "en": "when the app component renders for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 153.18,
          "en": "because during that render cycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 155.793,
          "en": "delete confirmation is also rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 157.29,
          "end": 159.552,
          "en": "Now to work around this issue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 159.552,
          "end": 162.57,
          "en": "we could simply render delete confirmation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 162.57,
          "end": 167.27,
          "en": "conditionally here, depending on modal is open, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 173.223,
          "en": "so that it's only rendered if modal is open is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 174.24,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "That would work around this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 176.61,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "and would make sure that this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 181.74,
          "en": "is not always set right at the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 181.74,
          "end": 186.74,
          "en": "A more elegant solution could be to render it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 189.63,
          "en": "but to then go into the modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 189.63,
          "end": 193.11,
          "en": "and not always output this children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 193.11,
          "end": 195.96,
          "en": "so that the app component doesn't have to deal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 195.96,
          "end": 197.97,
          "en": "with conditionally rendering this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 197.97,
          "end": 199.756,
          "en": "but instead it's the modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 199.756,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "where this might make more sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 205.53,
          "en": "so that here we can check if open is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 205.53,
          "end": 207.524,
          "en": "and if that's the case, we output the children,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.524,
          "end": 209.703,
          "en": "otherwise we render null here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 213.03,
          "en": "That would be an alternative solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.03,
          "end": 214.86,
          "en": "that should also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 218.13,
          "en": "that this timer is not set right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.13,
          "end": 220.73,
          "en": "and we can confirm this by simply console logging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.73,
          "end": 222.633,
          "en": "timer set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 227.07,
          "en": "If I console log this, save this, and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.07,
          "end": 229.2,
          "en": "I'm not seeing this in the log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 229.2,
          "end": 231.76,
          "en": "which proves that it's not set right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 236.91,
          "en": "but still this code here has a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 236.91,
          "end": 238.8,
          "en": "And to show you this problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.8,
          "end": 242.58,
          "en": "let me try to remove one of these items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.58,
          "end": 245.34,
          "en": "If I do that, you see the timer is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 245.34,
          "end": 248.964,
          "en": "and after three seconds the item was therefore removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.964,
          "end": 253.88400000000001,
          "en": "But if I remove it myself before these three seconds expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 253.88400000000001,
          "end": 257.4,
          "en": "this timer will also still expire",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.4,
          "end": 261.78,
          "en": "because we didn't stop it and that wasn't a problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 261.78,
          "end": 264.81,
          "en": "But it will be a problem if I click no",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264.81,
          "end": 267.75,
          "en": "because now you will see that even though I clicked no,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 267.75,
          "end": 271.53,
          "en": "after three seconds this item disappeared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.53,
          "end": 273.9,
          "en": "because the timer is never stopped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.9,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "when this component here is not rendered anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 280.5,
          "en": "Instead it was started and it keeps on going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.5,
          "end": 283.32,
          "en": "behind the scenes, independent from the question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 283.32,
          "end": 286.233,
          "en": "whether this component is currently visible or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 289.147,
          "en": "And that's of course a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 289.147,
          "end": 293.193,
          "en": "And it is a problem that can be fixed with useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}